          body:
            "A container is an isolated *process*, not a mini-VM: images package the filesystem in cached layers, start in seconds, and make the deployment unit equal to the test unit — which is their whole promise. Make images trustworthy with a checklist you can run: digest-pinned bases and honoured lockfiles for reproducibility, manifest-before-source ordering and multi-stage builds for cache and size, `.dockerignore` and runtime secret injection so context and credentials never enter a layer, non-root users, read-only filesystems and dropped capabilities for a real boundary, exec-form commands so signals reach your app, health probes that reflect dependencies without cascading, and CI scanning plus immutable digests so rollback is an address rather than a hope. The verification is deliberately mechanical — history, digests, hardened runs, stop timing — because a container whose properties you cannot test is not a package you can trust next year.",
